[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816675450","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105473#issuecomment-2816675450","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105473","id":2816675450,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n4w56","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T11:59:31Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T11:59:31Z","body":"`_update_process_callback()` seems to have more complex logic for determining processing. It will enable processing even if smoothing is disabled, when physics interpolation is active. The two methods should probably be merged into one, because they can still overwrite each other.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816675450/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816740140","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105473#issuecomment-2816740140","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105473","id":2816740140,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n5Ass","user":{"login":"rbaker87","id":1047829,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDc4Mjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1047829?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbaker87","html_url":"https://github.com/rbaker87","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbaker87/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbaker87/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbaker87/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbaker87/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbaker87/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbaker87/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbaker87/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbaker87/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbaker87/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T14:58:04Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T14:58:04Z","body":"> `_update_process_callback()` seems to have more complex logic for determining processing. It will enable processing even if smoothing is disabled, when physics interpolation is active. The two methods should probably be merged into one, because they can still overwrite each other.\r\n\r\nThe logic in `_update_process_internal_for_smoothing()` seems to have been entirely redundant. We don't really need to know if smoothing is enabled/disabled when determining the process_callback state. Maybe the previous implementation assumed that there was some way to end up with no state defined at all? I just pushed a new version with all calls to it being replaced with `_update_process_callback()` as it covers the same cases checked previously anyway.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816740140/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2832612269","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105473#issuecomment-2832612269","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105473","id":2832612269,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o1jut","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-26T20:57:39Z","updated_at":"2025-04-26T20:57:39Z","body":"> We don't really need to know if smoothing is enabled/disabled when determining the process_callback state. Maybe the previous implementation assumed that there was some way to end up with no state defined at all?\r\n\r\nThe previous implementation assumed that the camera only works in process callback and it was made before physics interpolation.\r\n\r\nWhile the code was outdated, it did have some merit. With your current changes, the camera will call `_update_scroll()` every frame, regardless if it moved or not. Scroll is already updated on `NOTIFICATION_TRANSFORM_CHANGED` if smoothing is disabled, so doing it every frame is just wasteful and redundant.\r\n\r\nAlthough there are multiple factors to be taken into account when enabling or disabling processing and I suppose it's difficult to get it right. `_update_scroll()` already checks whether camera is the current camera, so there is not much extra processing involved. Maybe it's fine this way.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2832612269/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833715562","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105473#issuecomment-2833715562","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105473","id":2833715562,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o5xFq","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T00:14:10Z","updated_at